# Chrysalis

1. **Authoritative rules** are in **`AGENTS.md`**. Read **`DESIGN.md`**, **`docs/UNIVERSAL-TRANSLATOR-CANON.md`** (canon + **D6442** translate-only + **D6447** no demo-only), **`docs/UNIVERSAL-CONVERSION-METHOD.md`** (**inventory first** — default agent method), **`docs/STRATEGIC-PLAN.md`** (locked path — do not deviate), **`docs/MIGRATION-OS.md`** (operator stack), **`docs/PAUSED-AND-MAINTENANCE.md`** (maintenance + paused index), and **`ROADMAP.md`** as required there. **WISP CWL fidelity** (filled proof): **`docs/WISP-CWL-CONSOLIDATED-PIPELINE.md`** + rule **`wisp-cwl-fidelity.mdc`**. Universal method rule: **`universal-conversion-method.mdc`**.
2. **True conversion only — never demo-only code (**D6447**).** Applies to **every language pair**, not WISP alone. Do not invent simplified login/dashboard/shells, parity façades, force-settled green holes, or helper apps that only look like the product. Lift origin or emit an honest hole. After convert: **sign in and test against origin**.
3. **Complete conversion (**D6448**).** Convert must run the honest hole-close loop until zero holes or fail incomplete — see `docs/COMPLETE-CONVERSION-PROTOCOL.md`. Do not stop after one convert-all pass.
4. **Success template (**D6448-ST**).** Hole zero alone is not enough — vendor islands, page chrome, closed overlays, idle labels, signed-in origin compare. Terminal settle ≠ ST green. See `docs/COMPLETE-CONVERSION-SUCCESS-TEMPLATE.md` · `pnpm run hub:complete-conversion-prove`.
5. User messages without **build/implement/add/fix** are usually **questions** — clarify against the strategic plan; do not fork unless the user explicitly amends the plan. **Translate only** — do not invent map engines, CDN dialects, or chrome absent from source (**D6442**).
6. After substantive changes, run **`pnpm test`** (or the smallest relevant package tests). Respect package boundaries (no circular dependencies; no oracle or environment shortcuts in generated or verify code).
